### 20.14 Mandatory Live Tests

- [ ] Normal data, no motion → `NONE_DETECTED`, no supervision, no alert
- [ ] Abnormal HR **with motion** → enters Supervision Mode, no immediate alert
- [ ] Supervision Mode: vitals normalize before timeout → exits cleanly, logged, no escalation
- [ ] Supervision Mode: abnormality persists past configured duration → escalates to Patient Confirmation
- [ ] Abnormal HR **without motion** → skips supervision, goes straight to Patient Confirmation
- [ ] Patient taps "I'm OK" within countdown → cancelled, logged, no escalation
- [ ] Patient taps "I Need Help" → immediately proceeds to Stage 1 (contact)
- [ ] No response before countdown expires → automatically proceeds to Stage 1
- [ ] Contact acknowledges within window → escalation stops at `CONTACT_NOTIFIED`, does not proceed to hospital
- [ ] Contact does not acknowledge within window → auto-escalates to `HOSPITAL_ESCALATED`, appears flagged in Hospital queue
- [ ] Situational/spontaneous/nocturnal/limited-symptom/recurrent panic categories each correctly classified from representative test data
- [ ] Insufficient data → `UNKNOWN`/`NONE_DETECTED`, never invented
- [ ] ML success → `engine_used: "ML"`; forced ML failure → `engine_used: "RULE_FALLBACK"`; both paths correctly drive supervision/escalation routing
- [ ] `confidence` and `model_version` stored correctly in both paths
- [ ] All escalation-stage transitions visible live via WebSocket to Patient, Caregiver, and Hospital dashboards
- [ ] LLM report includes panic classification and escalation timeline without diagnosing

