## FINAL ACCEPTANCE TEST — Full End-to-End Flow

Run live, on real devices, confirming each hop:

```
1. Threshold-breaching reading with MOTION DETECTED → /api/health →
   preprocessing → ML/rule engine → routes to Supervision Mode
2. Supervision Mode: vitals normalize → exits cleanly, no alert (test A)
   (Separately) Supervision Mode: abnormality persists past timeout →
   escalates to Patient Confirmation (test B)
3. Threshold-breaching reading with NO MOTION → skips supervision →
   Patient Confirmation directly
4. Patient Confirmation: "I'm OK" tapped → cancelled, logged (test C)
   (Separately) No response / "I Need Help" → escalates to Stage 1 (test D)
5. Stage 1: real call + real SMS fires to registered emergency contact,
   correct message content (name, vitals, GPS, timestamp)
6. Contact acknowledges → escalation stops at CONTACT_NOTIFIED (test E)
   (Separately) Contact does not acknowledge within window → auto-escalates
   to HOSPITAL_ESCALATED, flagged in Hospital queue (test F)
7. Real GPS + reverse-geocode attached and correct at every stage
8. Real WebSocket updates reach Patient/Caregiver/Hospital dashboards live
   at every supervision/escalation transition
9. Emergency resolved → final state persisted, appears in real history with
   full supervision/escalation timeline
10. Report requested → real LLM cites engine_used, panic_attack_type, and
    escalation timeline as decision-support, never diagnosis; forced LLM
    failure confirms template fallback still delivers a complete report
11. Full navigation pass (Phase 13.5) across all four roles, including all
    new Phase 20 screens — zero dead buttons, zero errors
12. Patient uploads a real medical record → appears in their list → viewable
    by Doctor with proper access
13. Patient adds/edits/removes an emergency contact → reflected immediately
    and used correctly in the next Stage 1 escalation test
```

**Nothing is complete until its portion of this exact flow has been observed working live.**

